#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157167 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157352 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "109b0bfb-10fe-5b31-adb2-be746ef71936" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting X as a Function of Y Using a Table of Values"}] :question/id #uuid "dfd30d6a-23f2-5304-8cb1-cc3a0f31463e" :question/math-academy-id "e-7820" :question/problem "Plot the graph of $x= \\dfrac{1}{2}y - \\sqrt y\\,$ by completing the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To graph this curve, we can start by calculating the value of $x$ for various values of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=0 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0-\\sqrt{0}=0 \\\\ y=1 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1-\\sqrt{1}=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y=4 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4-\\sqrt{4}=0 \\\\ y=16 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16-\\sqrt{16}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize these results in the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-\\dfrac12$ | $0$ | $4$ |\n\nSo, we have the following points:\n\n$$\n(0,0), \\quad \\left(-\\dfrac 12,1\\right), \\quad (0,4), \\quad (4,16).\n$$\n\nIf we plot these points and connect them with a smooth curve, we get the following graph:\n\n![](images/70/709bfcd1e69a0e4fd88d95fb9d8592de93921fad230b5f892059525871dc50fb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157168 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157353 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51ae30bd-569c-52dd-96a0-4244578db5bf" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting X as a Function of Y Given the Graph of the Corresponding Function"}] :question/id #uuid "1a638e6a-e5ab-5a60-81f5-2847e917b456" :question/math-academy-id "e-7821" :question/problem "The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below. Sketch  the graph of $x=f(y).$\n\n![](images/76/76268e0ba23b56af4c7215a4a44f459e6a3ea42454f53df1d39894df16513865.png)" :question/worked-solution "To plot the graph of $x=f(y),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and reflect it over the line $y=x,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/2e/2e11bec1e27fd59a1b4ea4e44070591acf5cd8fefebe6d5e1a46ef0be3f5129f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157169 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157354 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f2981f6-bfbf-5c1e-a4a2-2814dc24804a" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Quadratic Function Where X Is a Function of Y"}] :question/id #uuid "e6282f0a-7891-5261-968e-63aa42421d00" :question/math-academy-id "e-7822" :question/problem "Plot the graph of $x=-2y^2 - 3y.$" :question/worked-solution "To plot $x=-2y^2-3y,$ we will first plot the function $y=-2x^2-3x$ and then reflect it over the line $y=x.$\n\nThe curve $y=-2x^2-3x$ is a parabola. It has the following factored form:\n\n$$\ny = -x(2x+3)\n$$\n\nFrom the factored form above, we see that we have a negative parabola with roots at $x=0$ and $x=-\\dfrac32.$ Therefore, we get the following graph:\n\n![](images/c2/c2a1492655ff33a49bd21e911b13b99d67191a4cd39683f34fca4be295dda41a.png)\n\nNow, to get the curve $x=-2y^2-3y,$ we just have to reflect the curve $y=-2x^2-3x$ over the line $y=x,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/7f/7fbfb3fd5bbacbf1c974bf654e993a7203934db5d679bfaa89ddc0c54e39a7df.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157353 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51ae30bd-569c-52dd-96a0-4244578db5bf" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting X as a Function of Y Given the Graph of the Corresponding Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f68eb99-4872-508e-88b5-dede4e95c5d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/20/208f0c6aea457ccb10a4149a318cbba55f21582c3c0750c7f3b110cd79ae8a9e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557995} {:answer/id #uuid "7d4f1863-9b86-582e-9f3c-ddb7e7f4ae6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/36/366bf464a2