 just have to reflect the curve $y=-9{x}^{2}+7x$ over the line $y=x,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/34/344f13842043f5eb5e0db0db694cbc5801373fe36cfc81e9324e8d02fcba5ebb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157352 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "109b0bfb-10fe-5b31-adb2-be746ef71936" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting X as a Function of Y Using a Table of Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12ee0f13-1d8d-57df-bd04-cc7746f3002b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ef/ef474e9e7a59e29da3b7123617a80d812f82c27f8667146b7809c22b7f7226c3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557909} {:answer/id #uuid "45ac3456-b50c-58a3-9d24-81a805df53de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/58/58460d4429562bc0607775deb51e853329d806e8fcba5f7bdc19732e760fd056.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558005} {:answer/id #uuid "86c8eedc-e3db-5bb4-a1cc-6df762823b30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/04/04995bfe30f047a84c55f52a97f6a2ad9a649301cc855770b387050108002474.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558130} {:answer/id #uuid "b9192647-002e-5736-bdc0-d881fb907106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bf/bf29f22661398d5c963a78d39b9933c42f68071f98ad9676680d562e80a68e58.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558238} {:answer/id #uuid "cd083a00-a54b-57a1-a7ab-de2582e682fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4c260e4fcb664dd2eb3738a461938e44aa8b96b8ca6acb38d1119db7894a36e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86c8eedc-e3db-5bb4-a1cc-6df762823b30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/04/04995bfe30f047a84c55f52a97f6a2ad9a649301cc855770b387050108002474.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558130} :answer-field/id #uuid "c76bdfa1-89f9-5bce-8d5d-17b75468935a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3927d759-d3f3-597c-93a6-57d23bec620b" :question/math-academy-id "q-88516" :question/problem "Determine which of the following is the graph of $x=(2y+1)^{2}-6\\,$ by completing the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |" :question/worked-solution "To graph this curve, we can start by calculating the value of $x$ for various values of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=-\\frac{1}{2} & \\,⟶\\,x={[2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+1]}^{2}-6=-6 \\\\ y=0 & \\,⟶\\,x=(2\\cdot 0+1)^{2}-6=-5 \\\\ y=1 & \\,⟶\\,x=(2\\cdot 1+1)^{2}-6=3 \\\\ y=\\frac{3}{2} & \\,⟶\\,x={[2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2})+1]}^{2}-6=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize these results in the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $-5$ | $3$ | $10$ |\n\nSo, we have the following points:\n\n$$\n(-6,-\\frac{1}{2}),\\,(-5,0),\\,(3,1),\\,(10,\\frac{3}{2}).\n$$\n\nIf we plot these points and connect them with a smooth curve, we get the following graph:\n\n![](images/de/ded8b752a5acdd94b4e73a4cf7b301ed0d616b0cfd35896b5c9e5275fc8ca2ad.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558490 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157353 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51ae30bd-569c-52dd-96a0-4244578db5bf" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting X as a Function of Y Given the Graph of the Corresponding Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54ede07e-edf1-5974-92ae-ec92ea7eafac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :a